WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:03.340
From one piece to a collection you can sell safely.

2
00:00:03.690 --> 00:00:10.450
This is the video for module four of Bead Making and Simple Crafts: your collection, selling and next steps.

3
00:00:11.700 --> 00:00:23.130
One beautiful piece shows you can bead. A small, consistent collection shows you can run a business. You can make the same design again, to the same standard, in a predictable time.

4
00:00:24.380 --> 00:00:26.010
You will learn to batch your work.

5
00:00:27.260 --> 00:00:30.650
You will learn to show your pieces clearly, so buyers trust you.

6
00:00:31.900 --> 00:00:35.650
And you will learn to protect your money, then plan your next three months.

7
00:00:36.900 --> 00:00:44.560
Step one. Choose a theme that links the pieces, such as a colour story like Emerald and Gold, an occasion, or a technique.

8
00:00:45.810 --> 00:00:53.790
Step two. Choose three to five pieces that work together, like a necklace, bracelet and earrings. Sets raise the average sale.

9
00:00:55.040 --> 00:01:04.850
Step three. Write a pattern card for each design: the bead list with exact counts, the pattern as letters, the findings, the time taken and the full cost.

10
00:01:06.100 --> 00:01:15.340
Step four. Count out all the beads for all the pieces first, into separate small bowls or lids, one per piece. You notice at once if you are short.

11
00:01:16.590 --> 00:01:22.710
Step five. Do each stage across the batch. String all, then knot or crimp all, then inspect all.

12
00:01:23.960 --> 00:01:29.020
A small range made well sells better than a large range with uneven quality.

13
00:01:30.270 --> 00:01:39.740
Ngozi in Enugu takes about 15 minutes to make one bracelet from start to finish. Five, one by one, would take about 75 minutes.

14
00:01:40.990 --> 00:01:44.620
In a batch, she spends 15 minutes counting beads for all five.

15
00:01:45.870 --> 00:01:47.980
25 minutes stringing all five.

16
00:01:49.230 --> 00:01:51.900
And 15 minutes knotting and gluing all five.

17
00:01:53.150 --> 00:02:05.010
That is 55 minutes. She saves about 20 minutes per five bracelets, and all five come out identical. Her labour cost per piece drops, so her profit rises at the same price.

18
00:02:06.260 --> 00:02:12.980
Wipe the camera lens. Work near a window in daylight, and avoid the flash, which causes glare on crystals.

19
00:02:14.230 --> 00:02:20.410
Use a plain background, like white paper or a wooden board, and keep it the same for the whole collection.

20
00:02:21.660 --> 00:02:29.190
Take three photos per piece: the whole piece laid flat, a close-up of the beads and clasp, and the piece worn to show size.

21
00:02:30.440 --> 00:02:36.140
Crop and brighten a little, but never change the colours. The customer must receive what she saw.

22
00:02:37.390 --> 00:02:44.300
Write down the agreed design, size, colours, price and delivery date, and confirm it in a WhatsApp message.

23
00:02:45.550 --> 00:02:49.500
Ask for a deposit, often around half, before you buy materials.

24
00:02:50.750 --> 00:02:52.750
Send a sample photo for approval.

25
00:02:54.000 --> 00:03:02.000
Collect the balance before delivery, and include a short care note: remove before bathing, store in the pouch, keep away from perfume.

26
00:03:03.250 --> 00:03:11.570
Fake bank alert messages and fake transfer screenshots are common. Never release goods because of an SMS or a screenshot.

27
00:03:12.820 --> 00:03:17.840
Open your own banking or wallet app and confirm the money is really in your balance.

28
00:03:19.090 --> 00:03:26.280
And never share your PIN, password or one-time code with anyone, including people who say they are from your bank.

29
00:03:27.530 --> 00:03:39.520
To remember. Build a themed collection of three to five pieces. Write a pattern card for each. Batch your work. Take honest daylight photos. And always confirm payment in your own app.

30
00:03:40.770 --> 00:03:56.490
Now practise. Plan your collection and write your pattern cards. Make a small batch and keep a production log. Set up your WhatsApp Business catalogue with three pieces. Then build your portfolio and write a 90-day plan, with one focus each month.

31
00:03:56.840 --> 00:03:58.780
Continue with the lessons below.
